aquinas-providence-necessary.md:1: argue/readings: S3 is read 2 ways: aquinas-providence-necessary.logic.r3 has "prov_eternal" and "prov_eternal → prov_preexists" and "□(foreseen → happens)" and "foreseen ∧ □(foreseen → happens) → flows_necessarily"; aquinas-providence-necessary.logic.r3.2 and aquinas-providence-necessary.logic.r3.3 have "prov_eternal" and "prov_eternal → prov_preexists" and "foreseen → flows_necessarily"; they differ when only "the effect is foreseen by divine providence", "the providence of God is eternal", "divine providence pre-exists the effect" and "the effect flows from divine providence of necessity" are true, which the second allows
