aquinas-providence-necessary.md:1: argue/answered: S3: answered no, which keeps aquinas-providence-necessary.logic.r3, to: Suppose "the effect is foreseen by divine providence", "the providence of God is eternal", "divine providence pre-exists the effect" and "the effect flows from divine providence of necessity" are true and "necessarily, (if the effect is foreseen by divine providence, then the effect happens)" and "necessarily, (if the effect is foreseen by divine providence, then the effect happens)" are false. Is S3, "But the providence of God, since it is eternal, pre-exists; and the effect flows from it of necessity, for divine providence cannot be frustrated.", true then?
