aquinas-providence-necessary.logic.r3: argue/answered: U1: answered yes, which keeps aquinas-providence-necessary.logic.r3.2, to: Does the text's argument take this for granted, whether or not it says so: "if (divine providence pre-exists the effect and the effect flows from divine providence of necessity), then the effect has a per se cause, present or past, which it necessarily follows"? Answer yes if the author would accept it as part of the argument.
